{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1208942-inspirations-for-wod-cod-london","id":1208942,"title":"Inspirations for WoD/CoD London","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-19T10:53:48-07:00","id":1208942,"title":"Inspirations for WoD/CoD London","content":"I've been running WoD/CoD and other urban fantasy systems (mostly savage worlds) set in in London for over 20 years now and have collected different sources and inspirations for this setting in books, RPG's and and TV. Thought I'd share for anyone who was interested.<br /> <br /> <u><b>RPG's</b></u><br /> <br /> OWoD Isles of the Mighty, and Dark Ages Britain<br /> NWoD Shadows of UK<br /> The whole Cthulhu Britannica line from Cubicle 7 especially the London Box Set (all currently unavailable as pdf\u2019s as they retool the system)<br /> The Laundry RPG also from Cubicle 7 (and also currently unavailable in PDF due to system retooling)<br /> The Fireborn RPG from Fantasy Flight Games<br /> Mythic Britain RPG from Design Mechanics (for a great mystical-historical version of Arthurian myth based on dark ages Celtic Britain and not the late medieval romantic version)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Books</b></u><br /> <br /> Neverwhere by Neil Gaiman<br /> The Rivers of London series by Ben Aaronvitch<br /> The Skyscraper Throne series by Tom Pollack<br /> Good Omens by Neil Gaiman and Terry Pratchett<br /> The Courts of the Feyre series by Mike Shevdon<br /> The Rook by Daniel O\u2019Malley<br /> Burned man series by Peter McLean<br /> The Mists of Avalon by Marion Zimmer Bradley, and the Warlord Chronicles by Bernard Cornwell (again for more dark age celtic versions of the Arthur legend)<br /> Hellblazer and Constantine Comic Books<br /> Mr Norrell and Jonathan Strange by Susannah Clarke<br /> <br /> <br /> Other books set in a supernatural London: Haven't read these ones (life gets in the way!) but all potentially interesting<br /> <br /> Felix Castor series by Mike Carey<br /> Alex Verus series by Benedict Jacka<br /> Matthew Swift series and Magical Anonymous Series by Kate Griffin<br /> Shadow Police series by Paul Cornell<br /> Kraken, King Rat, and Un Lun Dun by China Mievelle<br /> No Hero by Jonathan Wood<br /> <br /> <u><b>TV and Movies</b></u><br /> <br /> Neverwhere<br /> Doctor Who<br /> Torchwood<br /> Sherlock<br /> Mi5 (Spooks in UK)<br /> Misfits <br /> The Fades<br /> Dog Soldiers<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12792,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","user":"scifirabbi","date":". 04-19-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12792-scifirabbi","name":"scifirabbi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T14:16:49-07:00","id":1211559,"title":"","content":"If you've never read it, I highly recommend Alan Moore and Eddie Campbell's From Hell (the graphic novel; not the film very loosely based on it). At least an entire chapter is taken up with an occult tour of Victorian London, complete with several pages of foot notes in the back. <br /> <br /> I also rather enjoyed Chaosium's Goatswood &amp; Less Pleasant Places sourcebook of Ramsey Campbell's British Mythos stories, and Pagan's PISCIS group from Delta Green: Countdown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"u